 cannot be overstated, as violations can lead to biased or inefficient estimates. For instance, if the assumption of homoscedasticity is violated (a condition known as heteroscedasticity), the standard errors of the estimates may be incorrect, leading to unreliable hypothesis tests and confidence intervals. Similarly, if the residuals are not normally distributed, the validity of inferential statistics derived from the model may be compromised.\n\nIn summary, the Least-Squares Principle is a cornerstone of regression analysis, providing a systematic approach to estimating relationships between variables by minimizing the sum of squared residuals. Its effectiveness hinges on the adherence to key assumptions, which, if violated, can significantly impact the reliability of the regression results. As such, econometricians must carefully assess these assumptions when applying the Least-Squares Principle to ensure robust and valid conclusions from their analyses.", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": [], "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": null}, "content_filter_results": {"hate": {"filtered": false, "severity": "safe"}, "protected_material_code": {"filtered": false, "detected": false}, "protected_material_text": {"filtered": false, "detected": false}, "self_harm": {"filtered": false, "severity": "safe"}, "sexual": {"filtered": false, "severity": "safe"}, "violence": {"filtered": false, "severity": "safe"}}}], "created": 1771166096, "model": "gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18", "object": "chat.completion", "service_tier": null, "system_fingerprint": "fp_f97eff32c5", "usage": {"completion_tokens": 545, "prompt_tokens": 297, "total_tokens": 842, "completion_tokens_details": {"accepted_prediction_tokens": 0, "audio_tokens": 0, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "rejected_prediction_tokens": 0}, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": 0, "cached_tokens": 0}}, "prompt_filter_results": [{"prompt_index": 0, "content_filter_results": {"hate": {"filtered": false, "seve